.TH CHMAP_DESTROY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
chmap_destroy \- destroy a hash map and set pointer to NULL
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chashmap.h>

chmap_destroy(hm);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Frees all resources associated with the hash map, including all
key-value pairs, and then sets the hash map pointer to NULL.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
hm   Hash map to destroy (set to NULL after destruction)
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Safe to call with a NULL pointer
Frees all keys and values
Frees every bucket collision chain and the bucket/slot array itself

The macro evaluates hm exactly once. It must be a modifiable lvalue,
such as a variable or an element of an array, so an expression with a
side effect, such as handles[i++], destroys and clears one element.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chmap_create (3),
.BR chmap_destroy_with_dtor (3)
